~ after_hr
Curator: Layoff order received. Congratulations. You have saved a department from becoming a spreadsheet footnote.
Player: Do I get paid now?
Curator: You get the next assignment. Corporate tradition.
=> END

~ before_finance
Curator: Finance. Mira's payroll account. Retrieve the corrected payment register.
Player: More numbers. Comforting.
Curator: Names and numbers are habits. Read the sources, build a tight pool, and don't query the entire fucking internet.
Player: Small dictionary. Small footprint. Got it.
=> END

~ after_finance
Curator: Payment register received. The amounts finally agree with the paperwork.
Player: A miracle in Finance?
Curator: Don't get sentimental. One archive copy left.
=> END

~ before_vault
Curator: Last target. Oleg, records custodian. The signed archive copy is in the Executive Vault.
Player: That sounds less like intern work.
Curator: The service is slower. The human is still human. Look for a memorable name, a year, and his favourite little punctuation mark.
Player: Then I submit the file and go home.
Curator: Submit the file first. We can negotiate the fantasy afterwards.
=> END

~ after_vault
Curator: Signed archive copy received. Three files, three accounts, one finished assignment.
Player: Is that the end of onboarding?
Curator: For today. Let me see how much of yourself you left on the servers.
=> END

~ ending
if Campaign.final_mark == "A"
	Curator: Clean work, trainee. Keep this up and I might learn your name.
elif Campaign.final_mark == "B"
	Curator: You got the files. Next time, leave less of yourself behind.
elif Campaign.final_mark == "C"
	Curator: Results delivered. Your footprints need their own fucking department.
else
	Curator: The job is done. Your discretion, on the other hand, needs urgent medical attention.
=> END
